From b086169e11fc390563817383ca089fb86ca9ba4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garra1980 <igor.zamyatin@intel.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 04:10:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add profile support in upstream LevelZeroRuntimeWrappers

The profiling cache flush fills a device scratch buffer four times the
size of the L3 cache with zeros, and the host now waits for the fill to
complete before the timed kernel is launched. The fill and the kernel are
submitted to different command lists, so without the wait the kernel can
start while the fill is still running.

Flush resources are allocated only when IMEX_ENABLE_CACHE_FLUSHING is set.
A device that reports no cache size disables flushing with a message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
